# Single source of truth for shellcheck exclusions. Passed explicitly via
# --rcfile by BOTH callers (the hypr-scripts-shellcheck flake check in flake.nix
# and scripts/hooks/pre-commit) so they cannot drift apart — the list used to be
# duplicated as a literal in both.
#
# Excluded by NAME rather than by lowering the severity floor, so that any future
# info-level finding still fails the build. All three are artifacts of the
# deliberate `source "$(dirname "$0")/x.sh"` pattern the hypr scripts must use:
# they are deployed flat into ~/.config/hypr and source each other at runtime.
#
#   SC1091  cannot follow a source path built at runtime
#   SC2034  monitors-detect.sh assigns variables its *consumers* read
#   SC2154  move-all-to-group.sh reads `fails`, which hyprctl-classify.sh sets
#
# These were the only findings when the gate was introduced, so it starts
# genuinely clean rather than muffled. Adding a code here needs a reason on the
# same line.
disable=SC1091,SC2034,SC2154
